  "slug": "bilayer-graphene-energy-spectrum-3476",
  "summary": "Four preprints from mid-November 2026 extend spectral and electronic-structure methods to trions, magnetically confined systems and long-range Hamiltonians.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is numerical computation of energy spectra and electronic states in quantum systems, with emphasis on basis construction and solver design. Two items address confined or low-dimensional settings: a field-adaptive Hermite discrete variable representation benchmarked on two-dimensional quantum dots in perpendicular fields against analytic spectra, and a finite-element and Gaussian expansion treatment of trion energy levels in bulk semiconductors across hole-to-electron mass ratios. The remaining two items concern electronic structure in extended materials. One integrates a Krylov-based quantum impurity solver, with adaptive circuits and machine-learned moment prediction, into charge self-consistent DFT+QDMFT, validated on bcc systems. The other introduces MLEH-LR, a machine-learning electronic Hamiltonian that adds long-range interactions and external fields, applied to boron nitride ribbons. What is new across the set is the extension of established spectral approaches to external fields, long-range terms and learned components, rather than a single shared physical model.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
